---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import WhatsAppLink from '../components/WhatsAppLink.astro';
import { solarSources } from '../data/solar';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Solar Financing & Commercial Tax Guidance | Incetekh Energy"
  description="Understand rooftop solar loans, compare borrowing costs and learn how commercial solar depreciation differs from a household subsidy."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Plan the investment"
    title="A clearer route to solar finance."
    description="Start with the installation quote. Then compare your own funds, eligible household subsidy and the total cost of borrowing."
  />
  <div class="container finance-copy">
    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Residential rooftop loans.</h2>
      <p>
        Indian Bank publishes a PM Surya Ghar rooftop loan scheme with loans up
        to ₹2 lakh for the up-to-3 kW category and up to ₹6 lakh for systems
        above 3 kW and up to 10 kW. Its published minimum contribution is 10%
        and 20% respectively, with repayment up to 120 months including any
        moratorium.
      </p>
      <p>
        Eligibility includes roof rights, adequate roof area, an electricity
        bill in the applicant's name and credit criteria. Rates are linked to
        the bank's current lending terms. Confirm the latest rate, eligibility
        and charges directly with the bank.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={solarSources.loan}>
        View Indian Bank's official solar loan
      </a>
      <p class="note">
        Source checked 30 September 2026. This is an independent lender option,
        not an Incetekh banking partnership or promise of approval.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Compare more than the EMI.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Ask for the total repayable amount, floating-rate terms, fees and any
          insurance costs.
        </li>
        <li>
          Check your upfront contribution and when subsidy is credited or
          applied to the loan.
        </li>
        <li>
          Compare the EMI with conservative savings; fixed electricity charges
          may continue.
        </li>
        <li>
          Confirm which equipment, taxes, structure, metering and civil work the
          quote includes.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Keep your recent bills, roof ownership/right-to-use documents, identity
        documents and installation quotation ready for the lender. Share
        sensitive financial documents directly through its official channel.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/solar-guide/#subsidy">
        Understand the household subsidy
      </a>
    </section>
    <section class="prose" id="commercial">
      <h2>Commercial solar: a different calculation.</h2>
      <p>
        The PM Surya Ghar household subsidy does not apply to commercial
        connections. The Income Tax Department's depreciation schedule lists
        solar power generating systems at 40% of written-down value.
        Depreciation reduces eligible taxable income; it is not a 40% refund of
        installation cost.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your ownership, use, tax position and time the asset is put to use
        affect the deduction. Ask your tax adviser to confirm the applicable
        treatment. Our calculator excludes any tax benefit from its savings and
        payback figures.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={solarSources.tax}>
        Read the official depreciation schedule
      </a>
    </section>
    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Get the system right first.</h2>
      <p>
        A free site visit helps establish suitable capacity and the equipment
        needed before you compare finance options.
      </p>
      <WhatsAppLink
        label="Talk to an expert"
        message="Hi Incetekh, I would like to discuss a solar installation quote before comparing finance options."
      />
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
  .finance-copy {
    max-width: 60rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }
  section {
    padding-block: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  li {
    margin-block: 0.75rem;
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
</style>
